### Screenshots, recordings, and evidence

Repro test, run with `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs` on the source build above:

```ts
import fs from "node:fs/promises";
import path from "node:path";
import { afterEach, describe, expect, it } from "vitest";
import { useAutoCleanupTempDirTracker } from "../../test/helpers/temp-dir.js";
import {
  getRuntimeAuthProfileStoreCredentialsRevision,
  noteRuntimeAuthProfileStorePersistedMutation,
} from "../agents/auth-profiles/runtime-snapshots.js";
import { activateSecretsRuntimeSnapshot, refreshActiveSecretsRuntimeSnapshotForConfig } from "./runtime.js";
import { asConfig, setupSecretsRuntimeSnapshotTestHooks } from "./runtime.test-support.js";

const { prepareSecretsRuntimeSnapshot } = setupSecretsRuntimeSnapshotTestHooks();
const tempDirs = useAutoCleanupTempDirTracker(afterEach);

describe("secrets refresh retry repro", () => {
  it("re-runs the exec provider on every retry while the credentials revision advances", async () => {
    const root = tempDirs.make("openclaw-refresh-retry-repro-");
    const callLogPath = path.join(root, "calls.log");
    const commandPath = path.join(root, "provider.sh");
    await fs.writeFile(
      commandPath,
      [
        "#!/bin/sh",
        `printf 'call\\n' >> ${JSON.stringify(callLogPath)}`,
        "cat >/dev/null",
        "sleep 0.2",
        `printf '{"protocolVersion":1,"values":{"models/openai":"sk-test"}}'`,
        "",
      ].join("\n"),
      { encoding: "utf8", mode: 0o700 },
    );
    const config = (port: number) =>
      asConfig({
        gateway: { mode: "local", port },
        secrets: {
          providers: {
            vault: {
              source: "exec",
              command: commandPath,
              passEnv: ["PATH"],
              timeoutMs: 20_000,
              noOutputTimeoutMs: 20_000,
            },
          },
        },
        models: {
          providers: {
            openai: {
              baseUrl: "https://api.openai.com/v1",
              apiKey: { source: "exec", provider: "vault", id: "models/openai" },
              models: [],
            },
          },
        },
      });
    const calls = async () =>
      (await fs.readFile(callLogPath, "utf8").catch(() => "")).split("\n").filter(Boolean).length;

    activateSecretsRuntimeSnapshot(
      await prepareSecretsRuntimeSnapshot({
        config: config(18789),
        env: { PATH: process.env.PATH ?? "" },
        includeAuthStoreRefs: false,
        loadablePluginOrigins: new Map(),
      }),
    );
    const initialCalls = await calls();

    // Stand-in for unrelated auth-store writes during preparation.
    const bump = setInterval(() => {
      noteRuntimeAuthProfileStorePersistedMutation(undefined, {
        credentialsChanged: true,
        stateChanged: false,
        profileIds: [],
      });
    }, 50);
    const revisionBefore = getRuntimeAuthProfileStoreCredentialsRevision();
    let settled = false;
    const pending = refreshActiveSecretsRuntimeSnapshotForConfig({
      sourceConfig: config(19001),
      includeAuthStoreRefs: false,
    }).finally(() => {
      settled = true;
    });
    await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 4_000));
    const callsWhileBumping = (await calls()) - initialCalls;
    const settledWhileBumping = settled;
    clearInterval(bump);
    const result = await pending;
    const totalCalls = (await calls()) - initialCalls;
    console.log(
      JSON.stringify({
        initialCalls,
        callsWhileBumping,
        settledWhileBumping,
        totalCalls,
        result,
        revisionAdvancedBy: getRuntimeAuthProfileStoreCredentialsRevision() - revisionBefore,
      }),
    );
    expect(settledWhileBumping).toBe(false);
    expect(callsWhileBumping).toBeGreaterThan(5);
    expect(result).toBe(true);
  }, 30_000);
});
```

Output:

```
{"initialCalls":1,"callsWhileBumping":19,"settledWhileBumping":false,"totalCalls":20,"result":true,"revisionAdvancedBy":79}
✓ secrets refresh retry repro > re-runs the exec provider on every retry while the credentials revision advances 4801ms
```

### Impact and severity

- Affected: Gateways with exec SecretRefs backed by a slow or rate-limited provider. A 1Password service account allows 1000 requests per day per account, shared by every service account in that account.
- Severity: high. One startup used the whole daily quota. After that, agent `main` sessions and the Control UI stayed unavailable, and any restart would fail at startup with exit 78, until the quota reset (~19 h).
- Frequency: observed once with full logs (2026-10-15). On 2026-09-02 the same daily limit ran out with about 484 of 1000 requests unexplained; I have not confirmed that it had the same cause.
- Consequence: provider quota exhausted, Gateway unusable.

### Additional information

- I have not confirmed what advanced the credentials revision in the live case. During the same window, the log shows the following for two other configured agents:
  - about one OpenAI OAuth refresh failure per minute: `OAuth token refresh failed for openai: Failed to fence every historical OAuth refresh peer. | Agent admission requires its host owner.`
  - `running startup:handler-prewarm` about 230 times per minute
  - about 2000 `SQLite read-only snapshot` lines per minute for those agents' databases
- Possible fix: share one `SecretRefResolveCache` across the passes of a single refresh call, so a retry re-reads auth stores but not providers. Also log each retry with which revision moved, and bound or back off the retries.
- Related:
  - #56217: crash-loop exhausts 1Password limits; a different path, through process restarts.
  - #168658: cold owners are never retried, and the 1Password resolver discards `op` stderr.
  - #171054: bounds the outer publication retry to 4 attempts; it does not touch this inner loop.
  - #70952 and #72278: dedup and memoization of provider lookups; both closed as not planned.

