## What Problem This Solves

`cron.add` accepted a CLI-backed model with `@<profileId>` while `cron.update` refused it with `invalid cron.update params: The selected automation account is unavailable.` `captureCronInferenceBinding` records no host account for a CLI-backed model — that backend owns its own login (#172794) — creation consumes that as success, the update path treated it as an unavailable account. The same update must not accept that edit for a job that already records an account: the store keeps that account on a model change its next run refuses.

| Finding | File:line | Change |
| --- | --- | --- |
| The update guard asked a different question than the capture owner | `src/gateway/server-methods/cron-input-validation.ts:335-350` (`captureCronUpdatedInferenceBinding`) | Resolve the selection once and skip capture only for a CLI backend **with no recorded binding**; a bound job keeps its rejection |

## User Impact

Operators can move an unbound automation onto a CLI-backed model again — the remedy `docs/automation/cron-jobs/troubleshooting.md:37` gives for "Automation has no recorded inference account". Automations that already record an account keep the actionable rejection instead of being accepted and then failing every run with `Automation candidate is incompatible…`, after the previous model had already been replaced.

## Why This Change Was Made

Classification: **behavior-completing**. `Precedent: #172794` made a CLI-backed model record no host account and touched only creation (`src/cron/inference-binding.runtime.ts:27-37`). `cron.update` reaches `captureCronUpdatedInferenceBinding` (`cron.ts:388`) whenever a patch carries `payload.model`; `context.cron.readJob` returns the stored row, so a binding is visible here. No option, config key, store field, or migration is added.

## Evidence

### Maintainer correction and verification

The landing review found one additional automatic-routing case: a default CLI auth order could mask an explicitly selected native profile. The correction forwards the selected profile into the existing runtime resolver, preserving the existing rejection instead of accepting an unavailable native account. Original contributor commits are retained.

- Regression through `cron.update`: fails on `47d9f563fb7` because a model edit is committed; passes with the correction.
- Corrected head `e203c63a6709247f974e9409464b0648249b5c3b`: `pnpm test src/gateway/server-methods/cron.validation.test.ts --maxWorkers=1` — **135 passed**, 26.57s Vitest / 28.44s command wall time.
- Targeted formatting, type-aware lint, `git diff --check`, production-core types, and the Gateway test-type shards passed. Exact-head CI supplies broad proof; earlier CI belongs to the earlier head.
- Independent full-candidate P0–P2 review: no actionable findings after the correction.
- Simplification: one added production argument; regression reuses the existing suite and model fixture. No new owner, storage, option, or compatibility path. Live model execution remains outside this validation-only proof.

### Original contribution evidence

Remote test host, tree from `git archive` of `upstream/main` (`824fde2bf`) with `@openclaw/fs-safe` 0.26.5 installed. `dist` was built in-tree with `scripts/build-all.mts`: tsdown succeeded and `dist/extensions/anthropic` — the plugin owning the `claude-cli` backend — loads (health: `plugins.loaded` includes `anthropic`, `errors: []`). That build later exits non-zero in `copy-bundled-plugin-metadata` on a missing acpx dependency, unrelated to this plugin.

Regression in the existing `cron.validation.test.ts` (no new files): an unbound CLI-backed edit is accepted; a persisted bound job's edit is rejected, stored model unchanged.

Focused unit run (`node_modules/.bin/vitest run --config vitest.config.ts src/gateway/server-methods/cron.validation.test.ts --maxWorkers=1`); base and candidate differ only in `src/gateway/server-methods/cron-input-validation.ts` (md5 `dc599b70…` → `9ca26dd2…`):

| Run | Result |
| --- | --- |
| Base | `Test Files 1 failed (1)`, `Tests 1 failed \| 133 passed (134)`, 74.28s |
| Candidate | `Test Files 1 passed (1)`, `Tests 134 passed (134)`, 73.66s |

Shipped Gateway trace (`startGatewayServer` + authenticated client driving `cron.add`/`cron.update`/`cron.get`/`cron.run`; raw logs kept). Each bound job proves its account in-run: before the edit its embedded run reached the provider layer (`Couldn't connect to the AI service`), not the "no recorded inference account" refusal.

| Tree | Job | Edit to CLI model with `@profile` | Persisted model | Next run |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `71bc89ec5` | bound, account proven present | accepted | changed to the CLI ref | `Automation candidate is incompatible with its recorded inference account and route.` |
| `47d9f563fb7` | bound, account proven present | rejected: `The selected automation account is unavailable.` | unchanged | not attempted |
| `71bc89ec5` | unbound CLI job | accepted | changed to the CLI ref | `Automation has no recorded inference account…` |
| `47d9f563fb7` | unbound CLI job | accepted | changed to the CLI ref | same |

This commit is the round-1 head on top of `71bc89ec5` (fast-forward; no amend or force-push). Base passes (refused), `71bc89ec5` fails (`expected "vi.fn()" to not be called at all, but actually been called 1 times`), `47d9f563fb7` passes.


